course: dictionary
lesson: 9882
title: Tadpole: a word with a life story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tadpole is a young frog or toad that has just hatched from an egg. You can work out a lot from the words around it. «Tadpoles breathe with gills» tells you they live in water, because gills are for breathing underwater.
explain: The clue «a tadpole becomes a frog» shows that a tadpole is not a frog yet. It is an early stage that changes. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: Words can also have a second, informal meaning. A tadpole can mean a very small child, as a joke or a fond nickname. To know which meaning is right, read the rest of the sentence and check what it is about: a pond, or a person.
fact: A tadpole is a young frog or toad that has just hatched from an egg.
fact: A tadpole lives in water, has a tail and breathes with gills.
fact: The frog life cycle is frogspawn (eggs), then tadpole, then froglet, then adult frog.
fact: Metamorphosis is the big change of body when a tadpole grows back legs, lungs, and loses its tail.
fact: Informally, a tadpole can mean a very small child.
exercise: «Tadpoles breathe with gills.» What do tadpoles breathe with? | *Gills | Their eggs | Lungs | Their tails only
exercise: In the frog life cycle, what comes just before the tadpole? | *Frogspawn | Froglet | Metamorphosis | Adult frog
exercise: What is a tadpole? | A type of pond weed | A kind of insect | A grown-up frog that lives on land | *A young frog or toad that has just hatched from an egg
test: What is the big change of body, when a young animal grows into its adult shape, called? | Learning to swim | Laying eggs in a jelly clump | *Metamorphosis | Catching insects
test: Where do tadpoles live? | On the tops of trees | Inside jelly clumps only | Underground in burrows | *In water
exam: «Losing ponds means losing frogs.» Why is this true? | Ponds are only where frogs sleep at night | Frogs cannot swim at all | Ponds only hold insects and no animals | *Tadpoles live in water, and adult frogs need damp land nearby
